Lab 6: Configuring IdM in a Geographically Distributed Topology
Objectives
By the end of this lab, students will be able to:

Understand the concepts and benefits of geographically distributed Identity Management (IdM) topologies
Install and configure multiple IdM servers across different geographic locations
Set up proper replication between IdM servers for data consistency
Configure DNS services for distributed IdM environments
Test high availability scenarios and failover mechanisms
Validate the distributed topology for redundancy and fault tolerance
Troubleshoot common issues in distributed IdM deployments
Prerequisites
Before starting this lab, students should have:

Basic understanding of Linux system administration
Familiarity with Red Hat Identity Management (IdM) concepts
Knowledge of DNS fundamentals
Experience with command-line interface operations
Understanding of network connectivity and firewall concepts
Completion of basic IdM installation and configuration labs
